  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "A circumferential weld attaching the liner which protects the bellows from direct steam flow within the expansion joint had failed, allowing the liner to displace downstream and subject the bellows to direct steam flow. The direct exposure of steam flow to the bellows resulted in increased local turbulence and vibration, leading to high cycle fatigue of the bellows.",
    "cause_code": "X",
    "category": "Other",
    "theme": "expansion joint liner weld failure -> bellows high-cycle fatigue -> unisolable steam leak",
    "provisional": false
  },
